  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $y=-\\frac{x}{2}+7?$",
  "worked_solution": "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nThe line $y=-\\frac{x}{2}+7$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=2x+19$ has a slope of $2.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=2x+19$ is perpendicular to the given line.",
